# GHL CLI keys. Members never need this file.
#
# Setup saves your keys in ~/.ghl-cli/keys.env (not here), straight from the clipboard:
#   ghl keys paste api-key          your GHL key (a Private Integration)
#   ghl keys paste workflow-token   the browser login token (docs/get-firebase-token.md)
# and your sub-account in ~/.ghl-cli/config.json:
#   ghl config set-location "<the address bar from inside your GHL sub-account>"
# Check them any time with: ghl doctor. Never paste a key into a chat.
#
# This template is for the optional .env next to the code, which only the ./ghl wrapper script
# in this folder loads. Anything set in the environment wins over ~/.ghl-cli.

# --- Required: GoHighLevel public API ---
# A Private Integration key made INSIDE your sub-account (Settings -> Private Integrations).
# Normally saved with: ghl keys paste api-key
GHL_API_KEY=pit-xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx

# Your sub-account (location) id: the 20 characters after /location/ in your GHL address bar.
# Normally saved with: ghl config set-location "<address bar>"
GHL_LOCATION_ID=YOUR_LOCATION_ID

# --- Optional: the workflow token, for building workflows ---
# The public GHL API can't create workflows, only read them, so building uses GHL's internal
# (unofficial) API with your browser login token. Get it with the console snippet in
# docs/get-firebase-token.md. Normally saved with: ghl keys paste workflow-token
GHL_FIREBASE_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# Optional: your agency's own GHL address, for editor links. ghl config set-location saves it.
# GHL_APP_DOMAIN=https://app.gohighlevel.com
